.Dd $Mdocdate: November 13 2026 $
.Dt VMDTRAY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vmdtray
.Nd traffic light for vmd virtual machines in the system tray
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm vmdtray
.Op Fl x
.Op Fl c Ar console
.Op Fl i Ar interval
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
docks into the system tray of the desktop and shows the state of the
.Xr vmd 8
virtual machines as a traffic light.
Every
.Ar interval
seconds it runs
.Dq Nm vmctl Cm status
and lights one lamp:
.Bl -tag -width "yellow"
.It green
Every virtual machine is running.
.It yellow
Some virtual machines are running and others are not, or one is stopping,
paused or waiting.
.It red
No virtual machine is running, none is configured, or
.Xr vmd 8
cannot be reached.
.El
.Pp
Clicking the traffic light with the left mouse button starts the virtual
machine manager in its own session.
.Pp
When the session bus has a StatusNotifierItem watcher, as on KDE Plasma,
.Nm
registers a StatusNotifierItem over D-Bus.
The tray then shows a tooltip that tells how many virtual machines are
running.
Otherwise it docks an X window through the freedesktop.org system tray
protocol over XEmbed, and puts that text in the window title.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar console
Run
.Ar console
when the traffic light is clicked.
It must be an absolute path.
The default is
.Pa /usr/local/bin/vmConsola .
.It Fl i Ar interval
Check the virtual machines every
.Ar interval
seconds, from 1 to 3600.
The default is 5.
.It Fl x
Use the XEmbed system tray protocol even if StatusNotifierItem is
available.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
.It Ev DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
The session bus where the StatusNotifierItem watcher is looked for.
If it is not set, the XEmbed protocol is used.
.It Ev DISPLAY
The X server to dock into with the XEmbed protocol.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/bin/vmConsola" -compact
.It Pa /usr/sbin/vmctl
queried for the state of the virtual machines
.It Pa /usr/local/bin/vmConsola
default virtual machine manager
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
runs until it is killed or loses its connection to the tray, and exits
>0 if an error occurs.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vm.conf 5 ,
.Xr vmctl 8 ,
.Xr vmd 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Leonardo Santagostini Aq Mt leonardo@santagostini.com.ar
